{"agent":"recover-8","data":{"by":"recover-8","evidence":{"budget_forced":"residual _COMMENT_BOUNDARY fixed; settle the 4 confirmed findings by re-reviewing the current tree to a clean round","chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"Given `echo $(echo case)\\ncase x in x) echo hi;; esac\\ngit push origin main`, the first `case` is an argument to `echo` inside the `$()`, not a `case` statement. `_find_body` sees that bare `case` word, and `_has_esac` searches the entire remaining raw text for a later `esac`; it finds the later real case statement's `esac` and wrongly runs `_case_end` from the argument. `_case_end` starts with `depth = 1`, the later real `case`/`esac` pair leaves `depth` at 1, so it returns `n`. `_scan` therefore never marks the later newlines as cut, `_logical_lines` returns one line, and `_split` treats the newline before `git push` as whitespace rather than a command separator, so `git push` is not emitted as a command. This is a forbidden command after a valid top-level case statement that the new guard should refuse.","digest":"80511f70dde0ee0e","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body / _has_esac","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body / _has_esac"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"For `echo $(( (1+2) ))#\"line1\\ngit push is data\\nline2\"\\necho allowed`, `_sub_body` treats the first single `)` inside the arithmetic expression as the close of the `$(( ... ))` expansion; it records the wrong index in `sub_close`, so the following `#` is taken as a comment. `_scan` then cuts the newline inside the real double quote and returns `git push is data` as a top-level line. In bash that `git push` is quoted data inside the argument to the first `echo`, not a command, so the guard would falsely refuse it.","digest":"eed579330ede5b80","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_sub_body","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_sub_body"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The descent loop is capped at 16 iterations, but `_substitutions` returns only the immediate `$()`/backquote bodies and the loop advances one level per iteration (`bodies = [s for b in bodies for s in _substitutions(b)]`). A forbidden command wrapped in 17 nested `$()` layers, for example `S_17` where `S_0 = \"git push origin main\"` and `S_n = f\"echo $({S_{n-1}})\"`, is missed: `_substitutions(S_17)` starts at `S_16`, and after the 16 passes the loop exits with `bodies == [S_0]` but without ever appending the `git push origin main` command list to `cmds`. Bash executes `git push` in that input, so `F.check` incorrectly returns `None` for a forbidden command at depth 17.","digest":"98f374a35a999c03","family":"deepseek","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_commands","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_commands"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_find_body` treats the first unquoted `)` as the end of a `$(` / `<( ` / `>(` / `$((` body, so a nested subshell or parenthesized arithmetic close is taken for the substitution close. `sub_close` then does not contain the `)` bash actually ends the expansion on, and `_comment` treats a following `#` as a comment. For `echo $( (echo hi) )#; git push origin main`, bash runs `git push origin main` (`#` is glued to the substitution word), but the scan records the body up to the `)` after `hi`, resumes on ` )#; git push...`, drops that tail as a comment, and `check` returns `None`. The same miss happens for `echo $(((1+1)))#; git push origin main`: `_sub_body` assumes the first `)` is immediately followed by the arithmetic’s outer `)`, so the real outer `)` is not in `sub_close` and the `#` hides `git push`.","digest":"cf4428ae1a25550a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Inside a double-quoted span the walker drops every backslash-newline and treats `'` as ordinary text, so it does not see a single-quoted body nested in `$(...)`. Given `echo \"$(echo 'a\\<newline>; git push origin main')\"`, bash keeps the backslash and newline inside the single quotes, so the child only echoes and never runs `git push`. `_strip_continuations` rewrites that to `echo \"$(echo 'a; git push origin main')\"`, `_scan` records a body whose `;` separates a real command, and `check` refuses a command bash does not run.","digest":"a9b059bcb50f4699","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_strip_continuations","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_strip_continuations"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The parameter `\"echo $(echo case)\\ngit push origin main\"` is an unclosed `$(` (there is no `)` after `case`, despite the comment). Bash parses the whole command before running it and exits with `unexpected EOF while looking for matching ')'`, so `git push origin main` never executes. The test still requires `_check` to refuse it, locking in a false positive of the same kind as the removed backquote case.","digest":"6557f94611ed32a7","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_forbidden_commands.py:test_refused_substitution_body_edge_cases","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_forbidden_commands.py:test_refused_substitution_body_edge_cases"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":3,"diff_chars":20263,"diff_sha":"87712885836068b07f837369e0cda5025fe3e1f6a53fe0fe7ba33a5a73e65c82","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":269.2,"family":"deepseek","findings":6,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"d0f21f0114cb232e","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-forbidden-guard-multiline-quote-bypass.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T06