{"agent":"recover-8","data":{"by":"recover-8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_case_end` never uses the new `_comment` check, so a `#` comment inside a case arm is still walked instead of skipped. For input `echo \"$(case x in x) # esac )<newline>git push origin main;; esac)\"`, bash runs `git push origin main` (`# esac )` is a comment); the guard's `_case_end` treats the comment text `esac` as the closing `esac`, returns before the real `esac`, and `_find_body` then closes the outer `$()` at the `)` inside the comment, dropping `git push origin main`, so `F.check` misses it.","digest":"eeb7550e81e2da6b","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_case_end","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_case_end"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new nested-substitution branch only handles backticks and `$()`, not process substitution `<(...)` / `>(...)`; the same gap remains in `_case_end`. Given `echo \"$(cat <(echo ); git push origin main)\"`, bash executes `git push origin main`, but `_find_body` sees the process substitution's closing `)` as the closing `)` of the outer `$()` and truncates the substitution body before `git push`, so `F.check` returns None.","digest":"944315022e413046","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_find_body"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `_comment` helper is only wired into `_find_body`; `_case_end` still has no `#` branch, so a comment inside a `case` arm is scanned char-by-char. Given `echo \"$(case x in x) # esac)\\ngit push origin main\\n;;\\nesac)\"`, bash executes `git push origin main` in the case arm, but `_case_end` sees the commented `esac` as the closing keyword, drops `depth` to 0, and returns with `k` on the following `)`. `_find_body` then takes that `)` (also inside the comment) as the end of the enclosing `$(...)`, so the scanned body stops before `git push origin main` and `F.check` returns None for the forbidden command.","digest":"f74195be0cfc196a","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_case_end","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_case_end"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The diff adds `<(`/`>(` handling only inside `_find_body` (via `_sub_body`), but `_scan` is the top-level scanner that builds the initial substitution bodies from the raw command. For input `cat <(git push origin main)`, `_scan` never passes the leading `<` to `_find_body`, so the process substitution body `git push origin main` is not recorded as a command; the whole string stays one command headed by `cat`, and `F.check` returns None even though bash runs `git push origin main`. The new regression test only covers a `<(...)` nested inside an outer `$()`, not this top-level case.","digest":"15528ba710d234d1","location":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_scan","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/forbidden.py:_scan"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":2,"delta_from":"9cbf0b01d49c3286070aec0ccdb9756796a7a826","delta_raised":["f74195be0cfc196a","15528ba710d234d1"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":8574,"diff_sha":"abb830740c8312cc1827497573160621f4d00151e416556eda60178f004d298e","diff_source":"delta review of 4 commits since 9cbf0b01d4","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1.4,"family":"deepseek","findings":4,"fix_round":true,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"aaf165b9d61e4d60","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-forbidden-guard-multiline-quote-bypass.critic.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261107T154207Z-d95c1845.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794065283.2588477,"family":"moonshot","gate":"critic","model":"kimi-for-coding-highspeed","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"kimi-k3"}],"review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"a346e384d05eccdd3bb968399f7462dff2fca933","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/forbidden.py":"100644 5980385ba9562861c41585761490f36796a781b2",